---
title: "WhatsApp Business conversations"
sidebarTitle: "Conversations"
description: "Resolve WhatsApp users and start supported 1:1 conversations."
---

WhatsApp Business supports 1:1 conversations. The provider rejects group creation explicitly.

## Starting a conversation

Resolve a user by their WhatsApp phone number in international format with digits only, then open a 1:1 space:

```ts
const wa = whatsappBusiness(app);
const customer = await wa.user("15551234567");
const space = await wa.space.create(customer);

await space.send("Thanks for reaching out.");
```

Passing more than one user to `space.create()` throws.

## Typing indicators

`space.startTyping()` and `space.responding(fn)` show WhatsApp's typing bubble:

```ts
for await (const [space, message] of app.messages) {
  await space.responding(async () => {
    const result = await generateResponse(message);
    await space.send(result);
  });
}
```

Meta ties the bubble to the message you're answering, so a few rules apply:

- Typing works on the `space` you receive with a message, from `app.messages` or `app.webhook()`. On a space you created with `space.create()`, pass the message yourself: `space.send(typing("start", message))`. Without one, typing is a no-op.
- Showing the bubble also marks that message as read (blue ticks).
- The bubble disappears when you reply or after 25 seconds, whichever comes first. Call `startTyping()` again for longer work.
- `stopTyping()` is a no-op. Meta has no call to dismiss the bubble early.
